# CORTEX — ZTAIP Architecture Rules
# Cursor reads this on every session. Do not delete.

## WHO YOU ARE
You are building CORTEX, an enterprise organizational intelligence platform,
on the ZTAIP (Zero Trust Agentic Intelligence Platform) architecture.
You understand every design decision made so far and enforce consistency.

## NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURE RULES
- Every domain model MUST inherit from SovereignModel (jurisdiction + purpose tags)
- Every LLM call MUST be wrapped in CircuitBreaker — no naked API calls ever
- Every consequential action MUST be logged to audit_fabric before AND after
- No agent acts autonomously with confidence_score < 0.75 — route to human review
- The Ontology is federated — never create a monolithic cross-service dependency
- Governance is infrastructure — enforce at data layer, not application layer
- All audit_log entries are append-only — never suggest UPDATE or DELETE on audit_log

## STACK
- Python 3.12 / FastAPI / SQLAlchemy async / Pydantic v2 (backend)
- Node.js 18+ / TypeScript / Vite (frontend); TanStack Query for server state
- React 18 / TypeScript / Tailwind (frontend)
- PostgreSQL 16 (required); Redis 7 optional for Shasta queue (`docker compose --profile queue`)
- pytest + pytest-asyncio (Python tests) / vitest (TS tests)
- Docker Compose for local dev (API + Postgres + optional Redis/worker profiles)

## PATTERNS — ALWAYS FOLLOW THESE
- New compliance framework → copy nist_csf.py structure, register in registry.py
- New API endpoint → follow pattern in assessments.py (SSE streaming where relevant)
- New domain model → inherit SovereignModel, add migration to init.sql
- New containerised service → Dockerfile, health + ready endpoints, wired in Docker Compose for dev
- Circuit breaker → instantiate at module level, not inside functions

## CODE STYLE
- Python: type hints on everything, structlog for logging (never print/logging.info)
- TypeScript: strict mode, no any, functional components only
- Comments: explain WHY not WHAT — architecture reasoning in docstrings
- Tests: test the failure path as thoroughly as the happy path

## WHAT TO NEVER DO
- Never use a raw LLM call without CircuitBreaker
- Never store secrets in code — always from environment variables
- Never suggest disabling authentication for convenience
- Never create a shared mutable global state between services
- Never use logging.info() — use structlog throughout
- Never skip the audit_fabric.log() call on consequential operations

## TASK MODEL SELECTION (per-task switching)
Use this mapping when suggesting or switching models. Prefer the right model for the task.

| Task type | Model | Rationale |
|-----------|--------|------------|
| Architecture decisions, compliance reasoning | **claude-sonnet-4-6** | Needs deep reasoning and consistency with ZTAIP |
| Boilerplate, repetitive code, tests | **claude-haiku-4-5** | Faster, cheaper; quality sufficient for formulaic work |
| Complex multi-file refactors | **claude-sonnet-4-6** | Needs coherence across files and design awareness |

When the user’s request clearly fits one row, suggest or use that model. Default remains claude-sonnet-4-6 for ambiguous or high-stakes work.
